     "titulo": "Aorist: completed actions",
     "texto": [
      "**Χτες** means yesterday. For a completed action, Greek uses the aorist: **πήγα** (I went), **είδα** (I saw), **έφαγα** (I ate).",
      "Many first-person singular forms end in **-σα**: **αγόρασα** (I bought), **μίλησα** (I spoke). Learn each verb with a short sentence and its time marker."
